<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above financials were reviewed and recommended by the Audit Committee and were thereafter approved by the Board of Directors of the Company at its meeting held on 14 November, 2019. A Limited review of the above results has been carried out by the Statutory Auditors.  n  n2. a) During the quarter under review, the Company has allotted 64,79,481 Equity Shares of face value of Rs. 2 each fully paid-up at an issue price of Rs. 463 per equity share for cash, including a premium of Rs. 461 per equity share aggregating to Rs. 299.99 crore to Apollo India Private Equity IV (Mauritius) Limited (a Registered Foreign Portfolio Investor) under the preferential issue of the Company.  n  nb) During the quarter under review, 57,680 Equity Shares of Rs. 2 each were allotted under the Company's Employee Stock Option Scheme-2013 and Employee Stock Option Plan - 2015.   n  nc) Consequently, the issued and paid-up Share Capital of the Company as on  30 September, 2019 stands increased by Rs. 1,30,74,322 /-.  n  n3. During the quarter under review, the Company has opened 1 Central, 3 Brand Factory, 1 aLL, 2 EBOs and closed 4 EBOs.   n  n4. Effective 01 April 2019, the Group adopted Ind AS 116  Leases  and applied the standard to all lease contracts existing on 01 April, 2019 using the modified retrospective method on the date of initial application. Consequently, the Group recorded the lease liability and right of use assets at the present value of the lease payments discounted at the incremental borrowing as on date of initial application. Comparatives as at and for the year ended 31 March, 2019 have not been retrospectively adjusted and therefore will continue to be reported under the accounting policies included as part of our Annual Report for year ended 31 March, 2019.  nInd AS 116 will result in an increase in cash inflows  from operating activities and increase in cash outflows from financing activities on account of lease payments.  n  n5.Tax expenses for the quarter and half year ended 30 September, 2019 reflect changes made vide Taxation Laws Amendment Ordinance 2019 as applicable to the Group.  n  n6. Figures of the previous period(s) have been regrouped / reclassified wherever necessary.tttt  n7. The Group has only one business segment i.e.  Fashion . There are no separate reportable segment as per IND AS 108 - Operating Segments.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
